# Copy to .env and fill in. Values are examples/placeholders only — never
# commit real credentials. This file documents the variables the app reads so
# a new deployment doesn't silently ship without them.
#
# Only the integrations that fail *silently* are listed exhaustively; add
# others here as they're introduced.

# ─── GoHighLevel (LeadConnector) ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# Used by lib/ghl.ts to upsert Early Access signups into GHL Contacts.
# If either of these is missing the signup still succeeds for the user, but the
# contact never reaches GoHighLevel — the failure is only visible in the server
# log ("[ghl] NOT CONFIGURED") and in the signup row's ghl_sync_error column.
#
# GHL_API_KEY     Private Integration Token for the sub-account, with the
#                 contacts.write scope (and contacts.readonly for the admin
#                 retry tooling). Starts with "pit-".
# GHL_LOCATION_ID The GHL location (sub-account) id contacts are upserted into.
GHL_API_KEY=pit-xxxxxxxx-xxxx-xxxx-xxxx-xxxxxxxxxxxx
GHL_LOCATION_ID=xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx

# ─── Cron endpoints ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Shared secret for the handlers under app/api/cron/*. They compare it against
# `Authorization: Bearer <CRON_SECRET>` and fail closed (401) when it is unset,
# so an unauthenticated caller can't burn provider quota.
#
# NOT REQUIRED TODAY: no cron is scheduled. The Vercel Cron entry for
# /api/cron/post-detection was removed from vercel.json because the Hobby plan
# permits only one cron run per day and rejects a five-minute schedule at deploy
# time. Set this when the project moves to Pro and the schedule is restored —
# see the header of app/api/cron/post-detection/route.ts.
CRON_SECRET=generate-a-long-random-string


